## std::time — Duration + Instant class shells + unix_ns free fn.
##
## Wave 2 (#06.8) — partial migration. Same shape as net / process:
## - `unix_ns() -> Int` fully migrates (lib block with c_symbol alias).
## - `class Duration end` / `class Instant end` are class shells; their
##   static-style constructors (`Duration.from_secs`, `Instant.now`, …)
##   still flow through the static-ctor fast path in
##   `mir/lower/expr/method_call.rs` and the runtime_table mangled-name
##   lookup until T#20 removes Duration / Instant from the carve-out.
##
## `unix_ns` is wall-clock (nanoseconds since 1970-01-01 UTC) and stays
## a bare Int-returning free fn until a `SystemTime` class lands. The
## monotonic `now_ns` free fn previously exposed here was removed in
## #06.5 T5.5 once `Instant.now` + `Instant.elapsed` covered every use
## case — the riven_time_now_ns C symbol is still linked (it backs
## `riven_instant_now`); it just is not reachable from Riven user code.

class Duration
end

class Instant
end

lib "riven_runtime"
  def unix_ns as "riven_time_unix_ns"() -> Int
end
